e for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Gabe Amo (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island's 1st District is a strongly Democratic seat, and first-term incumbent Gabe Amo is running for reelection with a large financial advantage. He has raised $1.7 million and holds $1.85 million on hand, while Republican Kellie Keenan has raised about $12,800. An independent candidate is also on the ballot but shows no signs of serious funding or organization.\n\nThe only recent poll, from Emerson College and WPRI in mid-October, gives Amo 54% to 26% among likely voters. Prediction markets put his chances at 99%. The race has drawn little attention, with local coverage describing it as quiet, and Amo has spent the fall touting federal funding and legislation. All available evidence points to a comfortable incumbent win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 21.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9965, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9933, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.987, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9871, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9901, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9942, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9904, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9911, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9934, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9926, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9925, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 22.1}, {"date": "2026-10-